  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance for Pension Reform in India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of the Grant is to assist the Government of India (GoI) to achieve optimal outcomes in pension reform by helping build institutional capacity in designing and implementing new pension schemes. The activities (the Activities) for which the Grant is given are as follows: (a)  Designing and introducing a fully funded, defined contribution pension scheme through specific analytical work, targeted training programs, workshops and conferences, and study tours. (b)  Developing and implementing a plan for the new pension scheme at the central level and building capacity to support implementation through inter alia training and consultant services. (c)  Developing and implementing plans for new pension schemes at the state level and building capacity to support implementation through inter alia training and consultant services.  This Project Code was initially set-up as an NLTA under P083669   , we are now reclassifying it with an IF code.</narrative>
  </description>
